  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nChamber of Commerce weather rounds out the weekend under the\nguise of building high pressure. Some afternoon cumulus fields\nhave sprouted overhead today, but is not expected to form into\nshowers or storms within our forecast area. A similar forecast\nsets up for the next several days while the surface high remains\nnestled over the region, allowing for a welcome reprieve from\nthe unsettled weather pattern we found ourselves in so far this\nmonth. \n\nCool temperatures and low humidity yields daytime highs spanning\nthe 60s to low 80s, elevation dependent, and overnight lows\ntumbling down into the 40s and 50s. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nHigh pressure will then become nudged offshore after midweek as\nupper level troughing swings into the Ohio Valley. Embedded\nshortwaves will promote periods of showers and storms for\nThursday onward. We could also see influence from a disturbance\nchurning off the eastern seaboard later on in the week. Whether\nan uptick in the risk for severe weather returning to the area\nwith these waves remains uncertain this far out in the forecast.\nSoil recovery that is anticipated to take place during the \nfirst half of the week should aid in limiting any initial \nflooding concerns. Heavy downpours and training storms will be \nclosely monitored, however, for localized issues heading into \nnext weekend.",
